#: includes/abilities/class-ai-abilities.php:32
msgid "Get VidShop AI status"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-ai-abilities.php:33
msgid "Everything needed before generating a video, in one call: whether this site is connected to the WPCreatix cloud, the plan and account email, the remaining credit balance, and every allowed generation duration with its exact credit cost and audio modes. It also answers the two derived questions directly, so nothing has to be inferred: `can_generate` says whether a generation can start right now, and `blocked_reason` says why not — \"not_connected\" (an administrator must connect the site in WP Admin first), \"options_unavailable\" (the cloud could not be reached) or \"no_credits\" (the balance is spent). The durations and credit costs returned here are AUTHORITATIVE and must never be hardcoded: they come from the cloud and can change without a plugin update. `vidshop/generate-video` requires an `acknowledge_credit_cost` value equal to the `credit_cost` of the chosen duration as read from this ability. This ability never fails because of the connection — a disconnected site, or one whose option lookup failed, still returns a complete payload with `can_generate` false. This ability contacts the WPCreatix cloud over the network (usage is cached for 60 seconds, generation options for 1 hour) and, if the stored Pro token has expired, silently re-exchanges the licence and rewrites the stored connection — so it is read-only from this site's point of view but it is not a purely local read."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-ai-abilities.php:53
msgid "Whether this site holds a valid connection to the WPCreatix cloud."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-ai-abilities.php:57
msgid "Connected plan, \"free\" or \"pro\". Null when not connected."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-ai-abilities.php:61
msgid "Email of the connected cloud account. Null when not connected, or when the site was connected with a Pro license."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-ai-abilities.php:65
msgid "Credits left on the account (subscription plus packs). Null when the balance is unknown, which is not the same as zero."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-ai-abilities.php:69
msgid "True only when the site is connected, the generation options resolved, and the balance is either unknown or above zero."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-ai-abilities.php:73
msgid "Why generation is blocked: \"not_connected\", \"options_unavailable\" or \"no_credits\". Null when nothing is blocking it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-ai-abilities.php:77
msgid "Selectable generation durations with their authoritative credit cost. Empty when the options could not be fetched."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-ai-abilities.php:83
msgid "Video length in seconds, passed as `duration` to vidshop/generate-video."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-ai-abilities.php:87
msgid "Credits this duration costs. Pass this exact number as `acknowledge_credit_cost` to vidshop/generate-video. Null when the cloud did not price it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-ai-abilities.php:91
msgid "Audio modes accepted for this duration, e.g. \"silent\" or \"music\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-ai-abilities.php:142
msgid "List VidShop AI generations"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-ai-abilities.php:143
msgid "The AI generation queue for this site, as { in_progress, recent, in_progress_count }. Each entry carries id, ai_call_id, product_id, title, status, video_id, duration_s, estimated_seconds, error, failure_code and created_at. The status ladder is pending -> processing -> importing -> imported | failed; \"failed\" spends no credits. An imported generation exists on this site as a DRAFT video — find it with vidshop/list-videos using origin \"wpcreatix_ai\", review it, then publish it with vidshop/update-video. This is a pure read: it does not poll the cloud and imports nothing. A background job already does that every minute, so a render that just finished can take up to a minute to appear here as imported."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-ai-abilities.php:179
msgid "Get VidShop settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-ai-abilities.php:180
msgid "Read-only view of the VidShop plugin settings: allow_anonymous_likes (whether logged-out shoppers may like a video) plus the currency-format overrides currency_position, price_thousand_sep, price_decimal_sep and price_num_decimals. A key that is absent, empty or null has never been overridden and is inherited from WooCommerce. There is deliberately no write counterpart: currency formatting is a display-wide setting with no agent use case, and a change would move every price on the storefront."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-generation-abilities.php:54
msgid "Trash video"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-generation-abilities.php:55
msgid "Moves a video to the trash. Reversible — use vidshop/restore-video to bring it back. Permanent deletion is not available through abilities."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-generation-abilities.php:63
msgid "ID of the video to trash. Read it from vidshop/list-videos."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-generation-abilities.php:72
msgid "Must be true. Confirms a human accepted that this video will be removed from every storefront until it is restored."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-generation-abilities.php:83
msgid "Always true — the video is now in the trash."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-generation-abilities.php:87
msgid "ID of the trashed video."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-generation-abilities.php:133
msgid "Generate video with AI"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-generation-abilities.php:134
msgid "Starts an AI video generation from a WooCommerce product. This spends cloud credits, which are real money. Read the allowed durations and their credit costs from vidshop/get-ai-status and never hardcode them — they change. The video is not returned here: the generation runs in the cloud and later arrives as a DRAFT video row, which vidshop/list-generations reports on."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-generation-abilities.php:142
msgid "WooCommerce product ID. Its featured image is used as the seed frame the video is animated from."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-generation-abilities.php:147
msgid "Optional free-text steer for the render, e.g. a mood or a detail to emphasise."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-generation-abilities.php:152
msgid "Clip length in seconds. Costs differ per duration — read them from vidshop/get-ai-status. Defaults to 8."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-generation-abilities.php:157
msgid "Audio mode. Shoppable feeds autoplay muted, so this defaults to silent."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-generation-abilities.php:161
msgid "Style template slug, e.g. \"auto\", \"studio-macro\", \"lookbook\". Defaults to \"auto\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-generation-abilities.php:165
msgid "Generate even when the product has no featured image. The result will not resemble the product — only set this when a human has accepted that."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-generation-abilities.php:172
msgid "Must be true. Confirms a human accepted that this generation spends credits."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-generation-abilities.php:177
msgid "The exact credit_cost for the chosen duration as reported by vidshop/get-ai-status. A boolean confirmation is set reflexively by a model; a number can only be obtained by having actually read the price."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-generation-abilities.php:188
msgid "Local generation row ID, or null when the row could not be written."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-generation-abilities.php:192
msgid "Cloud call ID for this render, or null when the cloud did not return one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-generation-abilities.php:196
msgid "Generation status at hand-off, usually \"pending\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-generation-abilities.php:200
msgid "Rough wall-clock estimate for the render, or null when unknown."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-generation-abilities.php:204
msgid "What to do next with this result."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-generation-abilities.php:239
msgid "The current credit prices could not be read from the cloud, so this generation was not started."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-generation-abilities.php:242
msgid "Prices are unknown right now, so the acknowledged cost cannot be checked. Read vidshop/get-ai-status and retry; if it also fails, the site is not connected or the cloud is unreachable."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: acknowledged credit cost, 2: actual credit cost, 3: duration in seconds.
#: includes/abilities/class-generation-abilities.php:256
#, php-format
msgid "The acknowledged credit cost (%1$d) does not match the current price (%2$d) for a %3$d second video."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-generation-abilities.php:263
msgid "The acknowledged credit cost does not match the current price. Read vidshop/get-ai-status again and retry with the value it reports."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-generation-abilities.php:295
msgid "Poll until this generation reaches imported or failed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-generation-abilities.php:370
msgid "A human must connect this site to VidShop AI in the plugin Settings screen. You cannot do this yourself."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-generation-abilities.php:385
msgid "This product has no featured image, so there is no seed frame to animate. Ask a human to add one. Retrying with allow_no_image set to true generates from text only, and the result will NOT match the product."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-generation-abilities.php:386
msgid "Generating without a featured image produces a video that does not match the product."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-storefronts-abilities.php:41
msgid "List Storefronts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-storefronts-abilities.php:42
msgid "List the saved VidShop storefronts. A storefront is a saved shortcode configuration — a chosen set of videos plus how they are presented — that the merchant renders on their own pages with [vidshop id=\"N\"]. Each row carries its decoded config object and a shortcode field, which is the ready-to-paste string for that storefront. Trashed storefronts are hidden unless status is set to trash."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-storefronts-abilities.php:46
msgid "Optional paging, search and ordering. Omit entirely to list the first page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-storefronts-abilities.php:50
msgid "Page of the collection to return. Defaults to 1."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-storefronts-abilities.php:55
msgid "Number of storefronts per page. Defaults to 20."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-storefronts-abilities.php:61
msgid "Limit results to storefronts whose name matches this string."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-storefronts-abilities.php:65
msgid "Limit results to one status. Omit to list everything except trashed storefronts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-storefronts-abilities.php:70
msgid "Field to sort by. Defaults to created_at."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-storefronts-abilities.php:75
msgid "Sort direction. Defaults to desc."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-storefronts-abilities.php:105
msgid "Update Storefront"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-storefronts-abilities.php:106
msgid "Rename a storefront, change its status, or replace its display configuration. Only the top-level fields you supply are written — but `config` is replaced wholesale, never merged, so always send the complete config object you read from vidshop/list-storefronts with your changes applied. The change takes effect immediately on every page carrying that storefront's shortcode, and the shortcode itself never changes — so a storefront can be retuned without touching any page content. Read vidshop/list-storefronts first to get the id and the current config."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-storefronts-abilities.php:110
msgid "The storefront id, plus the fields to change."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-storefronts-abilities.php:114
msgid "ID of the storefront to update."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-storefronts-abilities.php:119
msgid "New admin-facing name for the storefront."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-storefronts-abilities.php:123
msgid "New status. Setting trash hides the storefront and makes its shortcode render a missing-storefront notice."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-storefronts-abilities.php:128
msgid "The full display configuration to store. Selection keys: video_selection (\"all\" or \"specific\"), video_ids, orderby, order, tags, tags_operator. Presentation keys: layout, color_schema, columns.desktop, columns.tablet, columns.mobile, autoplay, loop, play_on_hover, show_arrows, show_dots, show_views, show_likes, auto_open_product_details, add_to_cart_action, post_add_to_cart_action, post_add_to_cart_url. The server re-sanitises the whole object through an allow-list, so any key not listed here is silently dropped and any missing key falls back to its default. Send the complete object, not a partial patch."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-storefronts-abilities.php:163
msgid "Get Analytics"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-storefronts-abilities.php:164
msgid "Read the VidShop performance report for a date range. Returns total and unique views, total and unique likes, total and average view time, add-to-cart and product-open totals, the top videos, the top added-to-cart products, a zero-filled per-day timeseries, library totals (videos, storefronts, products featured), and a previous block holding the same figures for the immediately preceding window of equal length so each stat can be compared. Site-wide reports also include a per_storefront rollup. Pass storefront_id to scope the whole report to one storefront; that variant adds a storefront identity block and omits per_storefront."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-storefronts-abilities.php:168
msgid "Reporting window and optional storefront scope. Omit entirely for the default window."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-storefronts-abilities.php:172
msgid "Named reporting window. Defaults to this_week. Use custom together with start_date and end_date."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-storefronts-abilities.php:177
msgid "Start of the window as YYYY-MM-DD, e.g. 2026-01-31. Required only when date_range is custom, and it must not be after end_date."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-storefronts-abilities.php:182
msgid "End of the window as YYYY-MM-DD, e.g. 2026-02-28. Required only when date_range is custom, and it must not be before start_date."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-storefronts-abilities.php:187
msgid "Limit the report to one storefront. Omit for the whole site."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: parameter name, 2: value supplied for it.
#: includes/abilities/class-storefronts-abilities.php:253
#, php-format
msgid "%1$s must be a real YYYY-MM-DD date for a custom date range, and \"%2$s\" is not one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-storefronts-abilities.php:259
msgid "Send start_date and end_date as YYYY-MM-DD, e.g. 2026-01-31, or drop them and use a named date_range such as this_month."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: start date, 2: end date.
#: includes/abilities/class-storefronts-abilities.php:270
#, php-format
msgid "start_date (%1$s) is after end_date (%2$s), so the custom date range covers no days at all."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-storefronts-abilities.php:276
msgid "Swap the two values: start_date must be the earlier date and end_date the later one."
msgstr ""

